&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F8xio1aaye1jxxxg8w0e7.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F8xio1aaye1jxxxg8w0e7.png" alt=" " width="800" height="448"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;When you're building a frontend, waiting for backend APIs or manually writing mock data can slow things down.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I wanted a simple place where I could get realistic API responses, generate test data, and create endpoints without setting up a backend. So I built &lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href="https://api.sonojs.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;SonoJS Mock&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It's a free set of tools for frontend development. Here's what's available:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Mock REST API
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Ready-to-use REST endpoints for users, posts, comments, products, photos, albums, todos, notifications, and countries.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Use them directly with &lt;code&gt;fetch&lt;/code&gt;, Axios, or any HTTP client. Shared resources are read-only in production.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://api.sonojs.com/docs" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Explore API documentation&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Temporary API
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Need your own API with writable data?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Paste your JSON, choose an expiration time (1, 6, 12, or 24 hours), and get a public endpoint. No account or backend setup required.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Supports GET, POST, PATCH, and DELETE.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://api.sonojs.com/temporary" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Create a Temporary API&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Fake Data Generator
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Generate up to 1,000 realistic JSON records for people, ecommerce, content, media, business, and location projects.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Copy the results, download them, or publish them directly as a Temporary API.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://api.sonojs.com/generator" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Try Fake Data Generator&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Image Generator
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Generate placeholder image URLs for avatars, thumbnails, profiles, banners, and more. You can use SVG placeholders or random real photos.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://api.sonojs.com/image-generator" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Open Image Generator&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Auth &amp;amp; JSON Workbench
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;There is also an authentication endpoint for testing login flows, plus a JSON Workbench currently in development with tools for formatting, searching, comparing, and converting JSON.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://api.sonojs.com/docs" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Explore the documentation&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href="https://api.sonojs.com/json" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Open JSON Workbench&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;p&gt;No installation, no account, and no backend required.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href="https://api.sonojs.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Give SonoJS Mock a try&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Feedback and suggestions are always welcome.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;A shared layout and four components that turn Tailwind classes into inline styles at render time — and why the pixel preset, not the class names, decides whether Outlook keeps your spacing.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  The Problem
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Your welcome email is a React component. It looks right in the browser, so you render it to a string and hand the string to your mail provider.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;WelcomeMail&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"mx-auto max-w-[600px] p-6 text-sm text-gray-700"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;h1&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"mb-4 text-2xl font-bold"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Welcome&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;h1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"mb-6"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Your&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;account&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;is&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;ready&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Sign&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;in&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;to&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;get&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;started&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;a&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="n"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"rounded-lg bg-teal-700 px-4 py-2 text-white"&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="n"&gt;href&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"https://example.com/dashboard"&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Open&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;dashboard&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;a&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Gmail web renders it. Outlook desktop renders a full-width white page with 12px text, no padding, and a link that looks like a link. Apple Mail renders the button but at a font size you never set. Nothing threw. The HTML is valid. The email is broken.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You try the three obvious fixes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Move every style into a &lt;code&gt;style&lt;/code&gt; object.&lt;/strong&gt; It works in Outlook, but now you maintain two styling systems, and &lt;code&gt;hover:&lt;/code&gt;, media queries, and &lt;code&gt;dark:&lt;/code&gt; have no object form.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;   &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;el&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;style&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;maxWidth&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;600&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;padding&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;24&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;fontSize&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;14&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Put the classes in a &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;style&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; block in &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;Head&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/strong&gt; Gmail web honors it. Outlook.com and the Gmail iOS app for third-party accounts drop it, so the mail arrives unstyled.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;   &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Head&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
     &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;style&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sb"&gt;`.card { padding: 24px; max-width: 600px; }`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;style&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
   &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Head&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Switch the whole thing to MJML.&lt;/strong&gt; You get reliable table markup, but you also get a second templating language. Props, types, and every shared component stop at the boundary, and your app logic has to be re-expressed as MJML includes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You want to author email in the same React and Tailwind vocabulary as the app, but clients only honor a narrow, inlined subset of CSS that the browser never had to explain to you.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The resolution is a layout that renders the same tree for every mail, with the design tokens in one place and a compile step that inlines them:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;EmailLayout&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;appName&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;previewText&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;supportMail&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;appName&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;previewText&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;supportMail&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;React&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;ReactNode&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Html&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;lang&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"en"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Tailwind&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="n"&gt;config&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
          &lt;span class="n"&gt;presets&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;pixelBasedPreset&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
          &lt;span class="n"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;extend&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;colors&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="no"&gt;TOKENS&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Head&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Body&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"bg-background text-foreground"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
          &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Preview&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;previewText&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Preview&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
          &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Container&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"mx-auto max-w-[600px] border border-border p-5"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
            &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
          &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Container&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Body&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Tailwind&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Html&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h2&gt;


  The Mental Model
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Think of a &lt;strong&gt;printing press with one plate&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Identity:&lt;/strong&gt; the JSX tree is the plate. It is the only original. The HTML you send is a print, and you can make as many prints as you like without redrawing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Update timing:&lt;/strong&gt; Tailwind classes are compiled when you run the press (&lt;code&gt;render()&lt;/code&gt;), not when the app builds. Change a class in the plate and the next print changes; the client never sees the class name.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Read timing:&lt;/strong&gt; clients read only what is physically on the page — inline styles. Anything left in a stylesheet is ink that never touched the paper.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Two consequences follow. First, a class that cannot be inlined (&lt;code&gt;hover:&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;group-hover:&lt;/code&gt;, complex selectors) cannot be trusted, no matter how good it looks in the preview. Second, the pixel preset is not cosmetic: without it, &lt;code&gt;p-6&lt;/code&gt; prints as &lt;code&gt;1.5rem&lt;/code&gt;, and the Word rendering engine behind Outlook desktop does not know what a &lt;code&gt;rem&lt;/code&gt; is.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The template is the plate; the inbox only ever sees the print.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  How to Use It
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Install React Email. The preview app ships separately.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;pnpm add react-email
pnpm add -D @react-email/ui
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;





&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;src/
└── mail/
    ├── components/
    │   ├── email-layout.tsx
    │   ├── email-button.tsx
    │   ├── email-heading.tsx
    │   ├── email-info-card.tsx
    │   ├── email-link.tsx
    │   └── index.ts
    ├── templates/
    │   ├── welcome-mail.tsx
    │   ├── reset-password-mail.tsx
    │   └── index.ts
    ├── mail.types.ts
    └── mail-service.tsx
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;src/mail/components/email-layout.tsx&lt;/code&gt; — one layout owns the palette, the width, and the footer:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Body&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Container&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Head&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Html&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
