&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;MailService&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"@/mail/mail-service"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;requestReset&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;mailService&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;MailService&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;request&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Request&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;mailService&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;sendPasswordResetMail&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;to&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"ada@example.com"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;userName&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Ada"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;resetUrl&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"https://ledger.dev/reset?token=abc"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;ipAddress&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;request&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;headers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;get&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"cf-connecting-ip"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;??&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;undefined&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;No app name, no support address, no subject. That is the payoff: a rename touches &lt;code&gt;MailConfig&lt;/code&gt;, and every template plus every subject line follows at once.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;❌ &lt;strong&gt;Do not make &lt;code&gt;appName&lt;/code&gt; optional and default it inside the template.&lt;/strong&gt; A defaulted &lt;code&gt;"App name"&lt;/code&gt; is what ships to a customer the day the config key is missing, and the preview app happily renders it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Pattern 2: Plug the service into a queue or a provider
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The service renders; something else delivers. Give it the smallest interface it needs and both a direct provider and a queue fit behind it.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Resend&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"resend"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;MailQueue&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"@/mail/mail.types"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="cm"&gt;/** Direct provider call: fine for a low-volume internal tool. */&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;createDirectQueue&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;apiKey&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;MailQueue&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;resend&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Resend&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;apiKey&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;sendMail&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;mail&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;resend&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;emails&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;send&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;mail&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="n"&gt;to&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;mail&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;to&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="n"&gt;subject&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;mail&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;subject&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="n"&gt;html&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;mail&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;html&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;??&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;""&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="n"&gt;text&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;mail&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;text&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

      &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="o"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;success&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;emailId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;success&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;message&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The key comes from the environment the caller already has, not from a module-scope &lt;code&gt;process.env&lt;/code&gt;. In a Worker that matters: secrets arrive on &lt;code&gt;env&lt;/code&gt;, and a module-scope read is evaluated once, before the binding exists.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Swap &lt;code&gt;createDirectQueue&lt;/code&gt; for a D1-backed producer and every template call site stays identical:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Env&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"@/mail/enqueue"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;enqueueMail&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"@/mail/enqueue"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;createMailService&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"@/mail/mail-service"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;buildService&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;env&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Env&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;createMailService&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;mailConfig&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="n"&gt;appName&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Ledger"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="n"&gt;systemMail&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"hello@ledger.dev"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="n"&gt;supportMail&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"help@ledger.dev"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;queue&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="n"&gt;sendMail&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;mail&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// One recipient row per email, so a fan-out becomes several rows.&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;to&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Array&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;isArray&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;mail&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;to&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;mail&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;to&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;mail&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;to&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;to&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;success&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"No recipient"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

        &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;emailId&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;enqueueMail&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;env&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;mail&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;to&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;success&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;emailId&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The service does not know whether a row was written or a provider was called, only that &lt;code&gt;sendMail&lt;/code&gt; resolves. That is the seam the companion post on D1 and Cloudflare Queues plugs into.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;MailQueue.sendMail&lt;/code&gt; returns the project's own &lt;code&gt;QueueMailResult&lt;/code&gt;, not a provider response, so the transport's shape never leaks into the template layer. The one field that needs care is &lt;code&gt;to&lt;/code&gt;: this interface allows &lt;code&gt;string | string[]&lt;/code&gt;, while a ledger with one recipient row per email needs a single address. Normalize at the adapter, not in the template.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Pattern 3: Preview every template without sending
&lt;/h3&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;pnpm &lt;span class="nb"&gt;exec&lt;/span&gt; email dev --dir=&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"src/mail/templates"&lt;/span&gt; --port=8088
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The preview app reads each default export and its static &lt;code&gt;PreviewProps&lt;/code&gt;. You edit a class, save, and see the print change. Nothing is sent, which is also the cheapest way to catch a broken prop.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Pattern 4: Assert the service, not just the template
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A template test proves the markup renders. A service test proves the two shared props actually reached it, which is the failure mode the preview cannot show.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;expect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;test&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"vitest"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;createMailService&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"@/mail/mail-service"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nf"&gt;test&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"every mail gets the configured app name and support address"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;let&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;sent&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;subject&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;html&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;undefined&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;service&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;createMailService&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;queue&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="n"&gt;sendMail&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;mail&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="n"&gt;sent&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;subject&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;mail&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;subject&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;html&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;mail&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;html&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;??&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;""&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;success&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;mailConfig&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="n"&gt;appName&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Ledger"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="n"&gt;systemMail&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"hello@ledger.dev"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="n"&gt;supportMail&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"help@ledger.dev"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;service&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;sendPasswordResetMail&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;to&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"ada@example.com"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;userName&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Ada"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;resetUrl&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"https://ledger.dev/reset?token=abc"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="nf"&gt;expect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;sent&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;subject&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;toBe&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Reset your password for Ledger"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nf"&gt;expect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;sent&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;html&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;toContain&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"help@ledger.dev"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nf"&gt;expect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;sent&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;html&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;toContain&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"https://ledger.dev/reset?token=abc"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;sendMail&lt;/code&gt; is a stub, so the test never touches a provider, a queue, or D1. It catches the three regressions that matter: a subject built from a hard-coded name, a footer that lost the support address, and a template that silently stopped rendering the action link.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;render&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"react-email"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;expect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;test&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"vitest"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;ResetPasswordMail&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"@/mail/templates/reset-password-mail"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nf"&gt;test&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"reset mail carries the action link and the expiry warning"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;html&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;render&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;ResetPasswordMail&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="n"&gt;userName&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Ada"&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="n"&gt;resetUrl&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"https://ledger.dev/reset?token=abc"&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="n"&gt;appName&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Ledger"&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="n"&gt;supportMail&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"help@ledger.dev"&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="nf"&gt;expect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;html&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;toContain&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"https://ledger.dev/reset?token=abc"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nf"&gt;expect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;html&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;toContain&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"expires in one hour"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;This one catches the failure the preview cannot: a prop that is accidentally required, renamed, or missing from one call site.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;❌ &lt;strong&gt;Do not put &lt;code&gt;render()&lt;/code&gt; behind a client component or a shared module.&lt;/strong&gt; It pulls in the server renderer. Keep it in a server-only file, or the bundler will try to ship React DOM server to the browser.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  When to Use It
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Reach for this setup only when all three are true:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You send more than one kind of email and want them to share a palette, spacing scale, and footer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You need HTML and plain text from a single source of truth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Your team already writes React and Tailwind, so the template is not a new skill.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Situation&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Better tool&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;One plain-text alert from a cron job&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;A template string&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;A marketing email designed by a non-engineer&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;A visual email builder&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Pixel-perfect complex layout with nested columns&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;MJML, or a builder that emits tables&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Per-locale copy for 20 languages&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Content files resolved before render, not 20 components&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Rendering user-supplied HTML&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Sanitize it; never render it as a template&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;A one-off mail whose copy changes every quarter&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Keep it in the service, but skip the shared layout&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Smell test: if a class you rely on cannot survive being pasted into a &lt;code&gt;style&lt;/code&gt; attribute, it is decoration in the preview and a bug in the inbox.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  How It Works Under the Hood
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;Tailwind&lt;/code&gt; is a render-time compiler, not a build step.&lt;/strong&gt; It walks the tree, collects the class names it finds, compiles those rules with Tailwind, and inlines the matching declarations onto each element. That is why &lt;code&gt;EmailLayout&lt;/code&gt; can hold the config: the config is read when the component renders, not when Vite builds.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;pixelBasedPreset&lt;/code&gt; swaps the scales to &lt;code&gt;px&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/strong&gt; Tailwind's spacing and type scales are &lt;code&gt;rem&lt;/code&gt;-based. The preset replaces both with &lt;code&gt;px&lt;/code&gt; values (&lt;code&gt;p-6&lt;/code&gt; → &lt;code&gt;padding: 24px&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;text-sm&lt;/code&gt; → &lt;code&gt;font-size: 14px; line-height: 20px&lt;/code&gt;). Outlook desktop's Word engine ignores &lt;code&gt;rem&lt;/code&gt; and inherited font sizing; this single preset is the difference between the design you drew and a wall of 12px text.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;render()&lt;/code&gt; returns a whole document, &lt;code&gt;toPlainText()&lt;/code&gt; returns a second artifact.&lt;/strong&gt; One tree, two outputs. If you build the text version by hand, the link in the text part is the first thing to drift.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Inlining covers most rules, and the leftovers are the ones that break.&lt;/strong&gt; React Email inlines declarations it can attach to a single element, and emits the rest into a &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;style&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; element inside &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;Head&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; — which is exactly why &lt;code&gt;hover:&lt;/code&gt; and media queries can look right in the preview and vanish in Outlook. There is no stylesheet specificity to fight, but there is also no &lt;code&gt;:focus&lt;/code&gt; and no descendant selector you can rely on. State-based styling has to become a prop (&lt;code&gt;isPrimary&lt;/code&gt;) or an inline color.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Every render costs CPU twice over.&lt;/strong&gt; Compiling the classes is work, and you do it once per email. A batch of 500 password resets compiles the same CSS 500 times. For high volume, render once per distinct prop set and reuse the HTML, or render at build time and store the artifact. In a Worker, that CPU is billed.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Phase&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;What exists&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;What the client sees&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Failure if skipped&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Author&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;JSX tree with class names&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Nothing&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;—&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Module load&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Component functions, token object&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Nothing&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Config drift between templates&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Service construction&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;code&gt;MailConfig&lt;/code&gt; with app/support&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Nothing&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Call sites invent their own names&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Render pass&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;React element tree&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Nothing&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;—&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Tailwind compile&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Rules for the classes used&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Nothing&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Unstyled classes&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Inline serialization&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;HTML with &lt;code&gt;style&lt;/code&gt; attributes&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;The layout&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Outlook ignores the stylesheet&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;toPlainText&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Text alternative&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;The fallback part&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;HTML-only mail, no link for text clients&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Preview render&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;A print that is thrown away&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Nothing&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Broken props ship&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Send&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Transport payload&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;The email&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;A beautiful mail nobody receives&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The discarded render is the preview: &lt;code&gt;email dev&lt;/code&gt; re-renders on every save and throws the result away. It is also the retry attempt in a queue consumer that re-renders a template instead of reusing the stored HTML. Store the artifact, not the component, once the mail is queued.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Server rendering note.&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;render()&lt;/code&gt; uses the server renderer under the hood. In a Cloudflare Worker that means &lt;code&gt;nodejs_compat&lt;/code&gt; in &lt;code&gt;compatibility_flags&lt;/code&gt;, because the Tailwind compiler and the renderer reach for Node built-ins. Do not import a template module into client code: the &lt;code&gt;render&lt;/code&gt; path and the Tailwind compiler are server-side dependencies, and the browser bundle needs neither.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compared to the built-ins.&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;renderToStaticMarkup&lt;/code&gt; from &lt;code&gt;react-dom/server&lt;/code&gt; gives you HTML and nothing else: no Tailwind compilation, no preview text handling, no text conversion. You would have to run Tailwind yourself at build time and inline the result. MJML gives you reliable tables, but its input is MJML XML, not React components, so props and shared app code cannot cross the boundary. React Email's limitation is the mirror image: it only inlines what Tailwind can express in a single element's &lt;code&gt;style&lt;/code&gt; attribute.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Conclusion
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The trade is a render-time compiler plus a thin service in exchange for one source of truth. You write the same React and Tailwind you already know, and you accept that the output is a print with a narrow vocabulary.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Put the palette, width, and footer in one layout; never restyle them per template.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Always enable &lt;code&gt;pixelBasedPreset&lt;/code&gt;, and treat any class that cannot be inlined as decoration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Let one service own &lt;code&gt;appName&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;supportMail&lt;/code&gt;, the subject, and the render, so a rename cannot leave a template behind.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Use this when you have a family of transactional emails and a team that already thinks in components. When you have one email that never changes, a plain HTML string is the boring, better answer.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;A boot script shorter than a tweet kills the reload flash — and the surprise is that React never owns the switch it paints with.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Applies to React 19 (&lt;code&gt;use&lt;/code&gt;), TanStack Start 1.x, and Tailwind CSS v4. On React 18, swap &lt;code&gt;use&lt;/code&gt; for &lt;code&gt;useContext&lt;/code&gt;; on Tailwind v3, use &lt;code&gt;darkMode: "class"&lt;/code&gt; instead of &lt;code&gt;@custom-variant&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  The Problem
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Your theme toggle is clean and correct after hydration.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// src/components/theme-toggle.tsx&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;useTheme&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"@/components/providers/theme-provider"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Theme&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"@/components/providers/theme-provider"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;choices&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"light"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"dark"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"system"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;ThemeToggle&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;setTheme&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useTheme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;select&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="n"&gt;aria&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;label&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Theme"&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="n"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="n"&gt;onChange&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;event&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;setTheme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;event&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;target&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;as&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;choices&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;map&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;choice&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;option&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;choice&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;choice&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
          &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;choice&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;option&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;select&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The stylesheet is equally simple:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight css"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;root&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nv"&gt;--background&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mh"&gt;#ffffff&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nc"&gt;.dark&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nv"&gt;--background&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mh"&gt;#09090b&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Now reload with "dark" saved. What the browser does:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;1. Server HTML arrives with &amp;lt;html class=""&amp;gt;.
2. The browser paints white, because --background is #ffffff.
3. The JS bundle downloads and React hydrates.
4. An effect reads localStorage and adds .dark to &amp;lt;html&amp;gt;.
Result: white → dark, on every reload, for every dark-mode user.
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Three fixes come to mind, and each one moves the problem.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Read storage during render.&lt;/strong&gt; React state seems like the natural home for a preference.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;   &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;setTheme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
     &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;localStorage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;getItem&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"theme"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;as&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;??&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"system"&lt;/span&gt;
   &lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;localStorage&lt;/code&gt; is undefined on the server, so rendering throws. In a client-only render, server HTML and first render disagree, and React patches the DOM after paint.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Move the read into &lt;code&gt;useEffect&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/strong&gt; It stops the crash but guarantees the flash: effects run after paint.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;   &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
     &lt;span class="nf"&gt;applyTheme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;localStorage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;getItem&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"theme"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;as&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;??&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"system"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
   &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Use &lt;code&gt;useLayoutEffect&lt;/code&gt; or hide the page until the theme is ready.&lt;/strong&gt; It cannot run before server HTML arrives, warns during server rendering, and hiding content trades the flash for a blank frame.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;   &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useLayoutEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
     &lt;span class="nb"&gt;document&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;documentElement&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;classList&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;add&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"dark"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
   &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You need the preference before the browser paints, and you need it inside React after hydration; a render-time read breaks the server, and an effect always arrives one paint too late.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The resolution is to put the decision in the HTML itself, as a tiny script that runs while the document is still parsing:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight html"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;script&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;try&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="kd"&gt;var&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;t&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;localStorage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;getItem&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"theme"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;t&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!==&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"light"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;t&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!==&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"dark"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;t&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!==&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"system"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;t&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"system"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="kd"&gt;var&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;d&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;matchMedia&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;matches&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="kd"&gt;var&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;t&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"system"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;d&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"dark"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"light"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;t&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="kd"&gt;var&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;e&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;document&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;documentElement&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="n"&gt;e&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;classList&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;add&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="n"&gt;e&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;style&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;colorScheme&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;catch&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;e&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;/script&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;That is the whole trick: the class is on &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;html&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; before any themed content can paint. React picks up the same choice after hydration, then stays in charge of later changes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  The Mental Model
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Think of a &lt;strong&gt;stage lightboard&lt;/strong&gt; with exactly two labeled sliders, &lt;code&gt;LIGHT&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;DARK&lt;/code&gt;. Only one can be up.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Identity:&lt;/strong&gt; the board is &lt;code&gt;document.documentElement&lt;/code&gt;. Its class and &lt;code&gt;colorScheme&lt;/code&gt; decide what the audience sees. React context holds the &lt;em&gt;note&lt;/em&gt; — the requested &lt;code&gt;Theme&lt;/code&gt; — not the position of the sliders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Update timing:&lt;/strong&gt; a stagehand sets the board before the doors open, using the note in their pocket. That is the inline script reading storage during HTML parse. Once the show is running, the director can move the sliders through &lt;code&gt;applyTheme&lt;/code&gt;, and a second stagehand can call out OS changes while the note says &lt;code&gt;system&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Read timing:&lt;/strong&gt; the lighting designer never reads the note; CSS reads only the board, at paint time. React reads the note at render time. When the note says &lt;code&gt;system&lt;/code&gt;, both readers resolve it through &lt;code&gt;matchMedia&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Two consequences. The board and the note can briefly disagree — &lt;code&gt;theme&lt;/code&gt; is &lt;code&gt;system&lt;/code&gt; while the board says &lt;code&gt;dark&lt;/code&gt; — and that is fine, because only one of them is authoritative for pixels. And if the pocket is empty or locked, the stagehand uses the default; the show still starts.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;CSS reads the switches; React reads the note.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  How to Use It
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Install the framework, icon, and menu pieces you need, then copy these files:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;pnpm add @tanstack/react-start @tanstack/react-router tailwindcss @base-ui/react lucide-react
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

