          &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;h2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"mt-4 text-slate-700"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;
          &lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"button"&lt;/span&gt;
          &lt;span class="n"&gt;onClick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;onClose&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
          &lt;span class="n"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"mt-6 rounded-md bg-slate-900 px-3 py-1.5 text-sm text-white"&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
          &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Done&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Resize no longer touches layout properties. A container query owns the card's typography. During drag, only a transform scales a preview ghost. &lt;code&gt;pointerup&lt;/code&gt; commits a data attribute the exporter reads. Animating &lt;code&gt;transform&lt;/code&gt; stays on the compositor; width and height writes do not. If &lt;code&gt;pointerup&lt;/code&gt; never fires, the attribute stays at the last commit and the ghost is discarded on the next frame.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight css"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;.slide-card&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nl"&gt;container-type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;inline-size&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nl"&gt;width&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;100&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kt"&gt;%&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nc"&gt;.slide-card__preview&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nl"&gt;transform-origin&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;top&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;left&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nl"&gt;will-change&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;transform&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nc"&gt;.slide-card&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;data-dragging&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"true"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;.slide-card__preview&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nl"&gt;animation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;nudge&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;180ms&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;ease&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;forwards&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;@keyframes&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nt"&gt;nudge&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;transform&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;scale&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;to&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;transform&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;scale&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mf"&gt;1.03&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;@container&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;min-width&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;480px&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nc"&gt;.slide-card__title&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;font-size&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mf"&gt;1.35rem&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;line-height&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mf"&gt;1.25&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The trade-off is measurement. Transforms do not change the layout boxes that HTML-to-PPTX converters inspect, so the export step must read the committed size attribute rather than &lt;code&gt;getBoundingClientRect&lt;/code&gt; after a scale. The focus trap is about forty lines and must be rechecked whenever the skill's generated heading structure changes, but without it keyboard and screen-reader order diverge the moment a modal opens. Container queries keep per-slide type scale local; the cost is skipping them in the static export path, where we flatten to explicit sizes so older print renderers stay predictable.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Theme regeneration is the other latency cliff. The agent client used for fallback tests is a standard OpenAI-compatible SDK with &lt;code&gt;baseURL: "https://b-lost.com/v1"&lt;/code&gt;. Under provider failover, a single slide's theme prompt stayed inside the same budget we already allow for one regeneration, so the editor did not need a special slow-path. Past that budget we keep the last committed theme and do not paint a partial palette. The skill remains responsible for scaffolding and export. The shell only refuses layout animation and keeps focus inside the dialog on screen.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The hardest call is which box is real. A live transform keeps the drag on the compositor, and a committed attribute is the only size the PPTX path will honor. Update the attribute during the gesture and you are back in layout thrash. Wait for &lt;code&gt;pointerup&lt;/code&gt; and a crash, a blur, or a killed tab can export the previous card. We log the miss and ship the last commit. That is the boundary: the skill may be non-deterministic; the shell may not guess.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Where do you freeze the box an exporter is allowed to believe when the pointer is still moving?&lt;/p&gt;
